<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>HelioForge Methodology | Model Coverage &amp; Research Limits</title><meta name="description" content="Understand HelioForge’s architecture coverage, bundled preview, local Python models, evidence boundaries and energy-research limitations."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta name="google-site-verification" content="wZk3bMiBHxDWxN4EmERLH9sBza2QlvsTaxbOSBncrvw"><meta name="author" content="Mohammad Rezwan Khan"><meta name="theme-color" content="#132923"><link rel="canonical" href="https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/domain.css"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="HelioForge"><meta property="og:title" content="HelioForge Methodology | Model Coverage &amp; Research Limits"><meta property="og:description" content="Understand HelioForge’s architecture coverage, bundled preview, local Python models, evidence boundaries and energy-research limitations."><meta property="og:url" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/"><meta property="og:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="HelioForge hybrid-energy research preview"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="HelioForge Methodology | Model Coverage &amp; Research Limits"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Understand HelioForge’s architecture coverage, bundled preview, local Python models, evidence boundaries and energy-research limitations."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://mkgrid.co.technology/social-preview.png"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website","name":"HelioForge","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/","publisher":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},"inLanguage":"en"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/#page","name":"HelioForge Methodology | Model Coverage & Research Limits","url":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/","description":"Understand HelioForge’s architecture coverage, bundled preview, local Python models, evidence boundaries and energy-research limitations.","inLanguage":"en","dateModified":"2026-10-26","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mkgrid.co.technology/#website"},"author":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/#person","name":"Mohammad Rezwan Khan","url":"https://mrkhan.co.technology/","sameAs":["https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan"]}}]}</script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/">H<span>↗</span> HelioForge</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/run/">Open app</a><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav></header><main id="main"><article class="document"><p class="eyebrow">HELIOFORGE / METHODOLOGY</p><h1>Know what the model represents.</h1><p class="lead">Hybrid-energy learning activities and research screens with explicit capability boundaries.</p><h2>Hosted preview and local calculations</h2><p>This website serves bundled examples and the Terminal workbench, which calculates new deterministic 24-hour energy-balance cases in the browser. It does not host the Python API. Advanced studies and optimization require the separate local application. The <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/START_HERE.md">local setup guide</a> explains how to run the separate research application on your own machine.</p><h2>Catalogue coverage</h2><p>The source catalogue includes 36 architectures, 24 scenarios and 36 architecture-linked lessons. In the local application, 19 architectures have runnable electricity-balance screens; 17 advanced architectures are explicitly study-only. There are 20 numerical scenario presets and four dynamic/control study presets. A displayed architecture is not evidence that all of its specialized physics have been implemented.</p><p>Browse original system layouts, read assumptions and follow the lessons’ experiment prompts and self-check questions. The hosted preview preserves these distinctions. The separate Terminal panel labels newly calculated reduced-model outcomes explicitly.</p><h2>Energy-model boundaries</h2><p>The hybrid hourly screen and the battery dispatch optimization are separate models. Their state-of-charge conditions, grid limits, units and energy-balance assumptions must be read in context. The <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/docs/HYBRID_METHODOLOGY.md">hybrid methodology</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/docs/METHODOLOGY.md">numerical methodology</a> are the detailed source references.</p><p>A demonstration day must not be multiplied into an annual business case without a reviewed annual model. A cheaper case that serves less demand is not automatically a better case. The interface’s geometry is explanatory; animated links are not solved electrical branch flows.</p><h2>Finance, forecasts and evidence</h2><p>Storage, project finance, PV, carbon and forecast examples are separate screening cases. No hidden automated revenue bridge connects them. Project and equity cash flows, nominal and real assumptions, and null or undefined metrics remain distinct. Synthetic examples are not calibrated forecasts, plant controls, investment recommendations or regulatory approvals.</p><h2>AI and review roles</h2><p>The public preview makes no external AI calls. The local application’s deterministic review mode is a checklist, not independently executed agents. Its optional external adapter requires explicit configuration and consent; it is not part of this hosted website.</p><h2>Separate synthetic wind-market model</h2><p><a href="https://mktrade.co.business/methodology/">MKTrade methodology</a> documents a separate synthetic wind-market model. Its illustrative market assumptions and results belong to a different project; they do not feed HelioForge’s bundled examples or models.</p><h2>Verification and reproducibility</h2><p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/QUALITY_REPORT.md">quality report</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/blob/main/docs/champion/VERIFICATION.md">release verification</a>, and inspect <a href="https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab/actions">CI runs</a>. The website’s source revision and runtime SHA-256 are in <a href="/app.json">app.json</a>. Software checks do not establish independent scientific calibration or operational approval.</p><p><a class="button primary" href="/run/">Explore the preview ↗</a></p></article></main><footer><a class="wordmark" href="/">HelioForge</a><p>Explore energy systems. Inspect their assumptions.</p><a href="https://mklab.co.technology/">Explore MKLab apps →</a></footer></body></html>